@startuml error_codes_mapping

title COOKie MVP - Error Codes Mapping & Middleware Architecture\nRFC 7807 Problem Details Standard

' Color coding for error severity
skinparam component {
  BackgroundColor<<ClientError>> #FFD700
  BackgroundColor<<AuthError>> #FFA07A
  BackgroundColor<<ServerError>> #FF6B6B
  BackgroundColor<<Middleware>> LightGray
  BackgroundColor<<External>> LightBlue
}

skinparam note {
  BackgroundColor #FFFFF0
}

' ==================================================
' Error Handling Middleware Pipeline
' ==================================================
package "ASP.NET Core Error Handling Pipeline" {

  component [Global Exception Handler\nMiddleware] <<Middleware>>
  component [Request Validation\nMiddleware] <<Middleware>>
  component [Authentication\nMiddleware] <<Middleware>>
  component [Rate Limiting\nMiddleware] <<Middleware>>
  component [RFC 7807\nProblem Details Factory] <<Middleware>>

  ' Client Errors (4xx)
  component [400 Bad Request] <<ClientError>>
  component [401 Unauthorized] <<AuthError>>
  component [403 Forbidden] <<AuthError>>
  component [404 Not Found] <<ClientError>>
  component [409 Conflict] <<ClientError>>
  component [413 Payload Too Large] <<ClientError>>
  component [422 Unprocessable Entity] <<ClientError>>
  component [429 Too Many Requests] <<ClientError>>

  ' Server Errors (5xx)
  component [500 Internal Server Error] <<ServerError>>
  component [503 Service Unavailable] <<ServerError>>

  ' External Dependencies
  component [Serilog Logger] <<External>>
  component [Sentry Monitoring] <<External>>
}

' ==================================================
' Middleware Pipeline Flow
' ==================================================

[Rate Limiting\nMiddleware] --> [Authentication\nMiddleware] : next()
[Authentication\nMiddleware] --> [Request Validation\nMiddleware] : next()
[Request Validation\nMiddleware] --> [Global Exception Handler\nMiddleware] : next()

' Error routing
[Rate Limiting\nMiddleware] ..> [429 Too Many Requests] : rate exceeded
[Authentication\nMiddleware] ..> [401 Unauthorized] : invalid token
[Authentication\nMiddleware] ..> [403 Forbidden] : insufficient role
[Request Validation\nMiddleware] ..> [422 Unprocessable Entity] : validation failed
[Request Validation\nMiddleware] ..> [400 Bad Request] : malformed request
[Global Exception Handler\nMiddleware] ..> [500 Internal Server Error] : unhandled exception
[Global Exception Handler\nMiddleware] ..> [503 Service Unavailable] : dependency failure

' All errors go through Problem Details Factory
[400 Bad Request] --> [RFC 7807\nProblem Details Factory]
[401 Unauthorized] --> [RFC 7807\nProblem Details Factory]
[403 Forbidden] --> [RFC 7807\nProblem Details Factory]
[404 Not Found] --> [RFC 7807\nProblem Details Factory]
[409 Conflict] --> [RFC 7807\nProblem Details Factory]
[413 Payload Too Large] --> [RFC 7807\nProblem Details Factory]
[422 Unprocessable Entity] --> [RFC 7807\nProblem Details Factory]
[429 Too Many Requests] --> [RFC 7807\nProblem Details Factory]
[500 Internal Server Error] --> [RFC 7807\nProblem Details Factory]
[503 Service Unavailable] --> [RFC 7807\nProblem Details Factory]

' Logging and monitoring
[RFC 7807\nProblem Details Factory] --> [Serilog Logger] : log all errors
[500 Internal Server Error] --> [Sentry Monitoring] : alert on 5xx
[503 Service Unavailable] --> [Sentry Monitoring] : alert on 5xx

' ==================================================
' RFC 7807 Problem Details Format
' ==================================================

note bottom of [RFC 7807\nProblem Details Factory]
  **RFC 7807 Problem Details Format:**

  Content-Type: application/problem+json

  {
    "type": "https://cookie.com/errors/{error-type}",
    "title": "Human-readable error title",
    "status": 422,
    "detail": "Detailed explanation for developers",
    "instance": "/api/v1/recipes/search?q=...",
    "timestamp": "2025-10-18T12:00:00Z",
    "trace_id": "abc-123-def-456"
  }

  **Extension fields (per error type):**
  - invalid_params[]: for validation errors (422)
  - retry_after: for rate limit / service unavailable (429, 503)
  - allowed_values[]: for enum validation errors
end note

' ==================================================
' Error Code Details
' ==================================================

note right of [400 Bad Request]
  **400 Bad Request**
  Malformed request syntax

  **Triggers:**
  - Invalid JSON body
  - Missing Content-Type header
  - Malformed query parameters
  - Invalid URL path segments

  **Example:**
  {
    "type": ".../malformed-request",
    "title": "Bad Request",
    "status": 400,
    "detail": "Request body is not valid JSON"
  }
end note

note right of [401 Unauthorized]
  **401 Unauthorized**
  Authentication required or failed

  **Triggers:**
  - Missing Authorization header
  - Invalid JWT token (malformed)
  - Expired JWT token
  - Revoked JWT token (in Redis blacklist)
  - Invalid refresh token

  **Example:**
  {
    "type": ".../authentication-required",
    "title": "Unauthorized",
    "status": 401,
    "detail": "JWT token has expired"
  }
end note

note right of [403 Forbidden]
  **403 Forbidden**
  Authenticated but insufficient permissions

  **Triggers:**
  - User role lacks required permission
  - Admin-only endpoint accessed by regular user
  - Account suspended or banned
  - Email not verified (for certain operations)

  **Example:**
  {
    "type": ".../insufficient-permissions",
    "title": "Forbidden",
    "status": 403,
    "detail": "Admin role required for this operation"
  }
end note

note right of [404 Not Found]
  **404 Not Found**
  Resource does not exist

  **Triggers:**
  - Recipe slug not found
  - User ID not found
  - Image ID not found
  - Recipe in draft/archived status (for public)

  **Example:**
  {
    "type": ".../resource-not-found",
    "title": "Not Found",
    "status": 404,
    "detail": "Recipe with slug 'xyz' not found"
  }

  **Security:** Do NOT reveal if
  resource exists for unauthorized users
  (prevents enumeration attacks)
end note

note right of [409 Conflict]
  **409 Conflict**
  State conflict with current resource

  **Triggers:**
  - Duplicate email on registration
  - Rating already exists (use PUT)
  - Recipe slug already taken
  - Concurrent update conflict (optimistic lock)
  - Database deadlock (after retries)

  **Example:**
  {
    "type": ".../duplicate-resource",
    "title": "Conflict",
    "status": 409,
    "detail": "Email already registered"
  }
end note

note right of [413 Payload Too Large]
  **413 Payload Too Large**
  Request body exceeds limits

  **Triggers:**
  - Image file > 5MB
  - Batch import > 100 items
  - Request body > 1MB

  **Example:**
  {
    "type": ".../payload-too-large",
    "title": "Payload Too Large",
    "status": 413,
    "detail": "Image file exceeds 5MB limit",
    "max_size_bytes": 5242880
  }
end note

note right of [422 Unprocessable Entity]
  **422 Unprocessable Entity**
  Validation failed on input data

  **Triggers:**
  - FluentValidation rule violations
  - Invalid field values (out of range)
  - Missing required fields
  - Invalid enum values
  - Business rule violations

  **Example:**
  {
    "type": ".../validation-error",
    "title": "Validation Failed",
    "status": 422,
    "detail": "One or more fields failed validation",
    "invalid_params": [
      {
        "field": "rating",
        "reason": "must be between 1 and 5",
        "value": 6
      },
      {
        "field": "comment",
        "reason": "must not exceed 500 characters"
      }
    ]
  }
end note

note right of [429 Too Many Requests]
  **429 Too Many Requests**
  Rate limit exceeded

  **Triggers:**
  - Public API: > 1000 req/hour per IP
  - Auth API: > 10 login attempts / hour
  - Upload API: > 50 uploads / hour
  - Brute-force protection triggered

  **Example:**
  {
    "type": ".../rate-limit-exceeded",
    "title": "Too Many Requests",
    "status": 429,
    "detail": "Rate limit exceeded. Try again later.",
    "retry_after": 3600
  }

  **Headers:**
  X-RateLimit-Limit: 1000
  X-RateLimit-Remaining: 0
  X-RateLimit-Reset: 1697625600
  Retry-After: 3600
end note

note right of [500 Internal Server Error]
  **500 Internal Server Error**
  Unhandled server exception

  **Triggers:**
  - Unhandled NullReferenceException
  - Database transaction failure
  - Serialization error
  - Configuration error
  - Bug in business logic

  **Example (production):**
  {
    "type": ".../internal-error",
    "title": "Internal Server Error",
    "status": 500,
    "detail": "An unexpected error occurred",
    "trace_id": "abc-123-def-456"
  }

  **Note:** NEVER expose stack traces
  or internal details in production.
  Log full details to Serilog + Sentry.

  **Development mode only:**
  Include stack trace and inner exception
end note

note right of [503 Service Unavailable]
  **503 Service Unavailable**
  Dependency failure

  **Triggers:**
  - PostgreSQL connection unavailable
  - Redis connection unavailable
  - Yandex Object Storage timeout
  - OAuth provider (Yandex/VK) down
  - Health check failure

  **Example:**
  {
    "type": ".../service-unavailable",
    "title": "Service Unavailable",
    "status": 503,
    "detail": "Database temporarily unavailable",
    "retry_after": 30
  }

  **Graceful Degradation Rules:**
  - Redis down: bypass cache, query DB
  - Object Storage down: queue upload
  - OAuth down: show email registration
  - DB down: return 503 with retry_after

  **See:** error_flow_database_failure.puml
  **See:** error_flow_redis_failure.puml
  **See:** error_flow_object_storage_failure.puml
  **See:** error_flow_oauth_failure.puml
end note

' ==================================================
' Custom Error Types (Business Logic)
' ==================================================

note bottom of [409 Conflict]
  **Custom Business Error Types:**

  **Authentication Errors:**
  - authentication-required (401)
  - token-expired (401)
  - token-revoked (401)
  - insufficient-permissions (403)
  - account-suspended (403)

  **Resource Errors:**
  - resource-not-found (404)
  - duplicate-resource (409)
  - resource-archived (410)

  **Validation Errors:**
  - validation-error (422)
  - invalid-file-format (422)
  - business-rule-violation (422)

  **Rate Limiting:**
  - rate-limit-exceeded (429)
  - brute-force-detected (429)

  **Infrastructure:**
  - internal-error (500)
  - service-unavailable (503)
  - database-unavailable (503)
  - cache-unavailable (503)

  All types prefixed with:
  https://cookie.com/errors/
end note

' ==================================================
' Logging Strategy
' ==================================================

note bottom of [Serilog Logger]
  **Logging Levels by Error Code:**

  **Information:** 2xx responses (sampled 10%)
  **Warning:** 4xx client errors (all)
  **Error:** 5xx server errors (all)
  **Critical:** repeated 503 (dependency down)

  **Structured Log Fields:**
  - trace_id: correlation ID
  - status_code: HTTP status
  - error_type: RFC 7807 type URI
  - endpoint: request path
  - user_id: authenticated user (if any)
  - duration_ms: request duration
  - ip_address: client IP (hashed)

  **Sentry Integration:**
  - Auto-capture 5xx errors
  - Include request context
  - Group by error_type
  - Alert on spike > 5 errors/minute
end note

' ==================================================
' Legend
' ==================================================
legend right
  **Error Severity:**
  |<back:#FFD700> Client Error (4xx) </back>| Client-side issue, fix request |
  |<back:#FFA07A> Auth Error (401/403) </back>| Authentication/Authorization |
  |<back:#FF6B6B> Server Error (5xx) </back>| Server-side issue, alert team |

  **Error Handling Principles:**
  1. All errors return RFC 7807 format
  2. Never expose internals in production
  3. Always include trace_id for debugging
  4. Log all errors with structured data
  5. Alert on 5xx via Sentry
  6. Graceful degradation for dependencies

  **Related Diagrams:**
  - error_flow_database_failure.puml
  - error_flow_redis_failure.puml
  - error_flow_object_storage_failure.puml
  - error_flow_oauth_failure.puml
endlegend

@enduml
